I’ll begin with the paper’s exact interchange definition, hardness/easy regimes, and—most importantly—the cost of producing a sequence certificate. I’ll only build if a native reconfiguration family survives G/H/V; otherwise I’ll leave a reviewable `REJECTED.md` with the mechanical-versus-compact cost comparison.
